# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vyom — environment variable template
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is git-ignored and must never be
# committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# PHASE 0: no variables are required. The application runs with none of these
# set. Each entry below is commented out and documents where it becomes
# required, so the structure exists before the phase that needs it.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the browser bundle and are PUBLIC.
# Never give a secret a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Application ------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute base URL of this deployment. Used for absolute links and callbacks.
# Optional locally; set it in Vercel for preview and production.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"


# --- Database (REQUIRED for any database work) ------------------------------
# Supabase Postgres. Both are SECRETS — server only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# Find them in Supabase: Project Settings → Database → Connection string.
#
#   DATABASE_URL  Transaction pooler, port 6543. Used by the application at
#                 runtime. Short-lived serverless connections need pooling.
#
#   DIRECT_URL    Direct connection, port 5432. Used by the Prisma CLI for
#                 migrations, which issue DDL and advisory locks that do not
#                 survive a transaction-mode pooler.
#
# The application still runs without these; only database code fails.
# See docs/database.md for the full setup walkthrough.

# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"


# --- Supabase Auth (REQUIRED for sign-in) -----------------------------------
# Find these in Supabase: Project Settings → API.
#
# Both are PUBLIC by design. The publishable key identifies the project and
# grants nothing on its own — every request it makes is constrained by Row
# Level Security. Publishing it in the browser bundle is the intended usage.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_..."

# Older projects issue an `anon` JWT instead. Either name works.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=""


# --- Testing ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Disposable PostgreSQL for the Row Level Security suite. `npm test` runs the
# tenant-isolation tests against it, and they write and delete rows — never
# point this at a database you care about.
#
# Start one with:
#   docker run -d --name vyom-test-pg -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres \
#     -e POSTGRES_DB=vyom_test -p 55432:5432 postgres:17-alpine
#
# RLS_TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:55432/vyom_test"


# --- Supabase service role (NOT USED YET) -----------------------------------
# SECRET — server only. Bypasses Row Level Security entirely.
#
# Nothing in the codebase reads this today, and that is deliberate: reaching for
# the service role is how tenant isolation gets quietly undone. If a future
# phase genuinely needs it, isolate that code and document why it must bypass
# RLS. Never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never import it into a client
# component.

# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""


# --- Nutrition datasets (Phase 8A) ------------------------------------------
# Directory the ingestion scripts read raw datasets and manifests from.
# Not a secret, but it is a local path — set it in .env.local, never commit one.
#
# Defaults to ./data/nutrition, which is git-ignored. Raw datasets are third-
# party files whose redistribution terms have not been reviewed; they must
# never be committed, put in public/, or uploaded to Supabase Storage.
#
# The web application never reads these files. Only the CLI does:
#   npm run nutrition:registry
#   npm run nutrition:import -- --manifest <file.json>
#
# See docs/nutrition-data.md.

# NUTRITION_DATA_DIR="./data/nutrition"


# --- Email (later phase) ----------------------------------------------------
# Transactional email for invitations and verification. SECRET — server only.

# RESEND_API_KEY=""


# --- Payments (Phase 16) ----------------------------------------------------
# Razorpay. The key ID is public; the key secret and webhook secret are not.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=""
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=""
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
